From: jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clusterlod: a lock-aware prune of whole components (clodConfig::simplify_prune_unlocked) and a per-group simplify report

ATOM-6, 2026-10-21. An edge collapse never removes a connected component, so a
group made of many small pieces (a leaf card is two triangles, a railing post a
closed box) cannot reach half its triangles: it is terminal or falls to the
sloppy fallback, and the chain ends there (Bistro: 168 of 722 DAG meshes ended
above 128 triangles, holding 175,151 of the scene's 281,632 coarsest).

clodConfig::simplify_prune_unlocked (default OFF = upstream's behaviour): after
the collapses, when a group is still above its target, remove WHOLE the
connected components of the group's input (welded by position) that carry NO
locked vertex of the LEVEL (the verify hook's per-group displacement locks hold a
vertex against a collapse, never a piece against its removal: they are marked
CLOD_LOCK_VERIFY), smallest first by clodMesh::component_extent (the caller's
per-vertex price; NULL = the component's box diagonal), until the target is met;
the group's error is raised to the largest price removed. A component touching
the group's border is locked by lockBoundary and stays (Nanite's
FCluster::SimplifyTriangles keeps it the same way); the next level's partition
moves the border. meshopt_SimplifyPrune is NOT used: it prunes by its own
quadric error regardless of locks (measured, ATOM-6 stage 0: 706 groups lost a
locked position, the facade's errors x16). A group may come out EMPTY: it is
output as a group with no clusters (the caller measures it).

THE SLOPPY FALLBACK IS REMOVED (simplify_fallback_sloppy, simplify_error_factor_sloppy,
simplifyFallback): vertex clustering ignored the locks and produced a wrong picture
with a huge error, and with the prune the bake measured 3 groups of 6,596 that
still took it; a group whose components are all locked and whose collapses miss
the target is accepted at <= simplify_threshold of its input or is terminal and
resolves at the next partition.

The report: clodGroup::simplify_flags (CLOD_SIMPLIFY_PRUNED),
locked_dropped (the level's locked positions the result no longer uses, by
weld) and pruned_relocked (vertices of pruned components the verify hook asked
to lock). The root group reports 0.

Applied at configure (irisgl/CMakeLists.txt) to a copy of the vendored header
in the build tree; the vendored file itself is never edited.
